{"slug": "peach-sorbet", "nyt_id": 10434, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/10434-peach-sorbet", "name": "Peach Sorbet", "author": "Jonathan Reynolds", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "1 quart", "min": 1, "max": 1, "yield_type": "volume"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 40, "raw": {"total": "40 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "10 to 12 ripe peaches, cut in half and pitted", "group": null, "quantity": 10.0, "quantity_max": 12.0, "unit": null, "item": "ripe peaches", "preparation": "cut in half and pitted", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 ¼ cups sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 1.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 cup water", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "water", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "3 tablespoons fresh lemon juice", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "fresh lemon juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "3 tablespoons light corn syrup", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "light corn syrup", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "½ teaspoon salt", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "In a saucepan over medium heat, poach the peaches in 1 cup of the sugar and the water until they are just tender, about 10 minutes. Remove peaches from the liquid and allow to cool. Place them in a blender and add the lemon juice, corn syrup, salt and the remaining quarter cup of sugar. Blend until smooth. If necessary, pass the peach mixture through a fine sieve."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Place the mixture in an ice cream machine and process according to